---
/* the about page: what Oro is, who it's for, how you learn, and the community */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { WHATSAPP } from '../lib/site.js';
---
<Layout url="about.html" title="About" description="Learn the skills cloud engineers use every day, in order. Oro is written for beginners and for people moving into cloud work from another job.">
<main class="about">
<header>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>Learn the skills cloud engineers use every day, in order. Oro is written for beginners and for people moving into cloud work from another job.</p>
</header>
<article class="md">
  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <p>No experience is needed to start.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Beginners:</strong> people new to tech. The first lessons start from the basics and explain new terms as they come up.</li>
    <li><strong>Career changers:</strong> people moving into cloud from support, development, networking or another field, who want a clear order to learn in.</li>
    <li><strong>Working engineers:</strong> people who use cloud tools already and want to fill the gaps underneath them, such as Linux, networking and how the cloud works.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How you learn</h2>
  <p>Each lesson explains what a tool does, why it exists and how to use it, with tasks to try as you read.</p>
  <p>Labs and projects run on your own computer. You don't need a cloud account or a credit card, and nothing you practise can run up a bill.</p>
  <h2>Community</h2>
  <p>Ask questions and share your progress in the <a href={WHATSAPP} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oro community on WhatsApp</a>.</p>
</article>
</main>
</Layout>
